            "created_at": "2025-08-30T06:43:43.20759+00:00",
            "notes": "Pharah feels pretty lacklustre right now, especially against counters. However, once you get this build going (around round 2-3), you'll be basically unstoppable.\n\nFor the first round, just try to earn as many points as you can. You're not going to do much with this build until you get a ton of AP, so I would recommend just jumping in on dps or healers and trying to at least get a trade.\n\nTaking [Blitz Barrage](item_b6bd0c8f-9bd2-4d3d-a353-1e70f74e131b) first means that you won't have your Jet Dash for mobility, so you'll be limited to only using her Concussive Blast to dodge or dive quickly. The upside is that you'll have a mini-barage that should help you get some easy trades and lots of damage to farm up points. If you're an experienced Pharah player and comfortable with her base kit, even against counter picks, then you can take [Recursion Battery](item_88c3fb1a-2d38-4d2c-b439-6aadd038fd1a) first to keep the Jet Dash and just play her normally. In that case, you would probably also want to build weapon power. \n\nI take [Winning Attitude](item_8714087c-c078-4619-a2ef-327bc6edaa69) because I know that I'll die in the first round a lot, especially if I'm up against Soldier or Cassidy, so I can at least get to my ult quickly off of the deaths for some impact later in the round.\n\nThis goes for all rounds, but for consistent damage with the mini-rockets, you really need to be directly above the target and as close as possible. Always aim at the ground beneath them.",
